Assemble with MASM 5.10

Microsoft's GW-BASIC source was written for MASM 1.x. MASM 5.10, the
assembler the rest of RetrOS uses, reads it the same way after these
changes, which alter no code:

- OEM.H: SHORT and LENGTH, switches nothing tests, are reserved words to
  MASM 5; the lines that set them are removed.
- BINTRP.H: the empty macro that marks a dispatch address as seen ended in
  "&endm", which MASM 5 does not take as the end of the macro, and the rest
  of every file that includes BINTRP.H was swallowed. An equate marks it.
- IBMRES.ASM: INSTR is a MASM 5 directive, so "T INSTR" and "Q INSTR" are
  written out; the routine INSTR becomes INSTRF (BISTRS.ASM, and the
  EXTRNs in GWDATA, GWEVAL, GWLIST, GWMAIN).
- GWDATA.ASM: three equates referred forward to labels, which MASM 5 does
  not allow; they move below the labels.

diff -ru a/BINTRP.H b/BINTRP.H
--- a/BINTRP.H	2026-11-13 15:59:31.243598726 -0500
+++ b/BINTRP.H	2026-11-13 15:59:31.244560015 -0500
@@ -115,8 +115,7 @@
     purge m
     n
 endm
-?&s macro
-&endm
+?&s = 0                 ; marks S as seen (MASM 5: was a macro)
 endm
 
 ;
diff -ru a/BISTRS.ASM b/BISTRS.ASM
--- a/BISTRS.ASM	2026-11-13 15:59:31.251443105 -0500
+++ b/BISTRS.ASM	2026-11-13 15:59:31.252560015 -0500
@@ -851,8 +851,8 @@
 ; I% IS RETURNED, UNLESS I% .GT. LEN(S1$) IN WHICH
 ; CASE 0 IS RETURNED.
 
-	PUBLIC	INSTR
-INSTR:	CALL	CHRGTR		;EAT FIRST CHAR
+	PUBLIC	INSTRF
+INSTRF:	CALL	CHRGTR		;EAT FIRST CHAR
 	CALL	FRMPRN		;EVALUATE FIRST ARG
 	CALL	GETYPR		;SET ZERO IF ARG A STRING.
 	MOV	AL,LOW 1	;IF SO, ASSUME, SEARCH STARTS AT FIRST CHAR
